\f1\fs22 \'93Do you know about the Dawkins?\'94 Cracker giggled, the alcohol warming his body and dulling his head. \'93Let me tell you about the Dawkins. You\'92ll love this story.\'94 Cracker spoke and as he became more intoxicated, he became increasingly loose with his tongue and told them everything of how much he loved Sarah, the bombing, the disc, the strange men on the travelator and their \cb3 love of evolution, science and reason\cb1 . He told them of The Dawkins and of the expected birth of The Dawkins 2.0, the one-after-the-one. When he had unloaded fully, he was spent and said, \'93Praise be to the Dawkins.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93\cb3 Tell me more about this evolution, man. It sounds great.\cb1 \'94 Elvis 1 said. \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Yeah. Evolution sounds like the real thing.\'94 Elvis 2 enthusiastically agreed. He had no choice but to agree with his doppelganger. Elvi not only looked the same, they thought the same. Exactly the same. Generally speaking, if you can convince one Elvis of something, you can convince them all. \'93I must know more of this Dawkins guy. He must have had it all together.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Wait a minute, I\'92ll get the others. They will want to hear about this.\'94 Elvis 1 proposed.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>He shortly returned with 4 more and by the end of the evening, Cracker had an audience of 20 Elvi transfixed by the evolution thing this Dawkins fellow had invented. Every Elvis that had worked in entertainment and hospitality, found it eminently plausible that their clients were related to monkeys. For the first time in his life Cracker was looked upon with admiration and it made him feel very uneasy. \cb3 They had broken out brain-dump caps and were downloading everything they could on evolution, science and reason\cb1 . The Chronicles of Dawkins etched into the brains of each Elvis before left he bar to go home. \

